1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,478
One worn part can stop a favorite routine.

2
00:00:03,598 --> 00:00:09,684
Useful electronics sit in drawers because
we don't know what to do with them.

3
00:00:09,804 --> 00:00:13,282
Orphan Parts Lens starts with two
questions: what

4
00:00:13,402 --> 00:00:16,880
do you have, and what do you want?

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,075
I make frappé coffee with this older
Hamilton

6
00:00:21,195 --> 00:00:25,270
Beach drink mixer, and its agitator is
worn.

7
00:00:25,390 --> 00:00:34,559
The rod has no model number of its own, so
the app asks which device it came from.

8
00:00:34,679 --> 00:00:38,754
The label under the mixer's base answers
that.

9
00:00:38,874 --> 00:00:45,496
Search the web then looks first for the
maker's own part, and keeps

10
00:00:45,616 --> 00:00:51,729
only pages the search returned, each as a
listing with its link.

11
00:00:51,849 --> 00:00:56,433
Check fit holds a listing against the
rod's measurements,

12
00:00:56,553 --> 00:01:01,138
and every unknown becomes a question for
the seller.

13
00:01:01,258 --> 00:01:07,880
Then I decide what to do with it: keep it
and fix it.

14
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:12,372
The same approach works for my unused
electronics.

15
00:01:12,492 --> 00:01:18,504
I catalog laptops, monitors and parts,
rate my skills, and say

16
00:01:18,624 --> 00:01:24,636
what I want from a build and what I can
spend.

17
00:01:24,756 --> 00:01:29,675
Muse Spark proposes projects from what I
own, and

18
00:01:29,795 --> 00:01:34,167
the rules keep only what my inventory
backs.

19
00:01:34,287 --> 00:01:40,845
I choose the tabletop arcade, and its
items are committed to it.

20
00:01:40,965 --> 00:01:48,070
Draw it shows how the finished build could
look, marked as a drawing.

21
00:01:48,190 --> 00:01:54,202
The missing controls become a Marketplace
search that I run myself.

22
00:01:54,322 --> 00:02:00,880
The build pack collects the items, the
steps, and the safety notes.

23
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:04,701
Next, a plan that adapts: a connection
diagram,

24
00:02:04,821 --> 00:02:08,522
and a different display that re-plans the
build.

25
00:02:08,642 --> 00:02:11,880
These are concept previews, not built yet.

26
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:19,007
On my phone, I capture photos and a spoken
note into the same inventory.

27
00:02:19,127 --> 00:02:23,631
Muse Spark, SAM 3.1, Muse Voice Transcribe
and Muse

28
00:02:23,751 --> 00:02:28,256
Image do the reading, the searching and
the drawing.

29
00:02:28,376 --> 00:02:32,880
And anyone can try it on my own photos.

30
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,556
Orphan Parts Lens.

31
00:02:35,676 --> 00:02:37,380
Find replacements.

32
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:39,204
Discover reuse.

33
00:02:39,324 --> 00:02:41,880
Build something useful.

